isites","0. Prerequisites",[191,208,209,210,215],{},"This guide assumes you have a working Kubernetes cluster and a Helm client installed. If you haven't set up a Kubernetes cluster yet, please refer to the ",[195,211,214],{"href":212,"rel":213},"https:\u002F\u002Fkubernetes.io\u002Fdocs\u002Fsetup\u002F",[199],"Kubernetes installation guide",".\nYou can use any Kubernetes cluster, including local clusters like Minikube or KinD, or cloud providers like GKE, EKS, or AKS.",[203,217,219],{"id":218},"_1-add-helm-chart-repo","1. Add Helm Chart Repo",[191,221,222],{},"Add the FiveNet Helm chart repository to your Helm client:",[224,225,230],"pre",{"className":226,"code":227,"language":228,"meta":229,"style":229},"language-bash shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","helm repo add fivenet https:\u002F\u002Ffivenet.app\u002Fcharts\nhelm repo update\n","bash","",[231,232,233,255],"code",{"__ignoreMap":229},[234,235,238,242,246,249,252],"span",{"class":236,"line":237},"line",1,[234,239,241],{"class":240},"sBMFI","helm",[234,243,245],{"class":244},"sfazB"," repo",[234,247,248],{"class":244}," add",[234,250,251],{"class":244}," fivenet",[234,253,254],{"class":244}," https:\u002F\u002Ffivenet.app\u002Fcharts\n",[234,256,258,260,262],{"class":236,"line":257},2,[234,259,241],{"class":240},[234,261,245],{"class":244},[234,263,264],{"class":244}," update\n",[203,266,268],{"id":267},"_2-create-a-namespace","2. Create a Namespace",[191,270,271],{},"Create a dedicated namespace for FiveNet if you do not already have one:",[224,273,275],{"className":226,"code":274,"language":228,"meta":229,"style":229},"kubectl create namespace fivenet\n",[231,276,277],{"__ignoreMap":229},[234,278,279,282,285,288],{"class":236,"line":237},[234,280,281],{"class":240},"kubectl",[234,283,284],{"class":244}," create",[234,286,287],{"class":244}," namespace",[234,289,290],{"class":244}," fivenet\n",[203,292,294,295],{"id":293},"_3-get-the-latest-valuesyaml","3. Get the Latest ",[231,296,297],{},"values.yaml",[191,299,300,301,303],{},"Retrieve the default ",[231,302,297],{}," file for the Helm chart to start configuring your deployment:",[224,305,307],{"className":226,"code":306,"language":228,"meta":229,"style":229},"helm show values fivenet\u002Ffivenet > values.yaml\n",[231,308,309],{"__ignoreMap":229},[234,310,311,313,316,319,322,326],{"class":236,"line":237},[234,312,241],{"class":240},[234,314,315],{"class":244}," show",[234,317,318],{"class":244}," values",[234,320,321],{"class":244}," fivenet\u002Ffivenet",[234,323,325],{"class":324},"sMK4o"," >",[234,327,328],{"class":244}," values.yaml\n",[203,330,332,333],{"id":331},"_4-configure-valuesyaml","4. Configure ",[231,334,297],{},[191,336,337,338,340,341,344,345,349,350,354,355,358],{},"Edit the ",[231,339,297],{}," file to suit your deployment needs. For details about the ",[231,342,343],{},".fivenet.config"," section, refer to the ",[195,346,348],{"href":347},"..\u002Fconfiguration\u002Fconfig-reference#must-set-config-options","configuration reference page",", specifically the ",[351,352,353],"strong",{},"\"Must Set Config Options\""," section and reference list at the top, to create a working ",[231,356,357],{},"config.yaml"," for FiveNet.",[191,360,361],{},"At a minimum, you should review the FiveNet configuration, secrets, persistence, and how the deployment should be exposed in your cluster.",[203,363,365],{"id":364},"_5-install-or-upgrade-fivenet","5. Install or Upgrade FiveNet",[191,367,368,369,371],{},"Deploy or update FiveNet in your Kubernetes cluster using the configured ",[231,370,297],{}," file:",[224,373,375],{"className":226,"code":374,"language":228,"meta":229,"style":229},"helm upgrade --install fivenet fivenet\u002Ffivenet \\\n  --namespace fivenet \\\n  -f values.yaml\n",[231,376,377,395,404],{"__ignoreMap":229},[234,378,379,381,384,387,389,391],{"class":236,"line":237},[234,380,241],{"class":240},[234,382,383],{"class":244}," upgrade",[234,385,386],{"class":244}," --install",[234,388,251],{"class":244},[234,390,321],{"class":244},[234,392,394],{"class":393},"sTEyZ"," \\\n",[234,396,397,400,402],{"class":236,"line":257},[234,398,399],{"class":244},"  --namespace",[234,401,251],{"class":244},[234,403,394],{"class":393},[234,405,407,410],{"class":236,"line":406},3,[234,408,409],{"class":244},"  -f",[234,411,328],{"class":244},[203,413,415],{"id":414},"_6-verify-the-deployment","6. Verify the Deployment",[191,417,418],{},"After the Helm release is installed, verify that the workloads are starting correctly:",[224,420,422],{"className":226,"code":421,"language":228,"meta":229,"style":229},"kubectl get pods -n fivenet\nhelm status fivenet -n fivenet\n",[231,423,424,439],{"__ignoreMap":229},[234,425,426,428,431,434,437],{"class":236,"line":237},[234,427,281],{"class":240},[234,429,430],{"class":244}," get",[234,432,433],{"class":244}," pods",[234,435,436],{"class":244}," -n",[234,438,290],{"class":244},[234,440,441,443,446,448,450],{"class":236,"line":257},[234,442,241],{"class":240},[234,444,445],{"class":244}," status",[234,447,251],{"class":244},[234,449,436],{"class":244},[234,451,290],{"class":244},[191,453,454,455,457,458,461,462,465],{},"Ensure that FiveNet is externally reachable as configured in your ",[231,456,297],{}," file, for example through your configured ",[231,459,460],{},"Ingress",", ",[231,463,464],{},"Service",", hostnames, and TLS settings.",[203,467,469],{"id":468},"_7-post-installation-steps","7. Post-Installation Steps",[191,471,472,473,477],{},"After installation, follow the ",[195,474,476],{"href":475},"post-install-steps","post-installation steps"," to complete the setup.",[479,480,482],"h3",{"id":481},"troubleshooting","Troubleshooting",[191,484,485,486,490],{},"For common issues during Kubernetes or Helm installation, such as database-related errors, refer to the ",[195,487,489],{"href":488},"..\u002Fconfiguration\u002Fcommon-installation-issues","Common Installation Issues"," page.",[492